module Core


### Resolves an end-relative offset `^offset` against a container `count`.
### This free routine is the lowering target of the `^n` back-index syntax
### (`list[^1]`, `text[^3]`, the open-ended slice bound `text[a til ^0]`).
### `^` is pure syntax sugar carrying no runtime type: `OperatorLoweringPass`
### rewrites each `coll[^n]` subscript to `coll.getitem!(back_resolve(count: coll.count(), offset: n))`.
### `^1` resolves to `count - 1` (the last element); `^0` resolves to `count`
### (one-past-the-end, valid only as a slice bound).
### :param count: The container length used as the reference point.
### :param offset: The end-relative offset where `1` means the last element.
### :returns: The resulting forward `U64` position.
### :throws: {IndexOutOfBoundsError} when `offset > count`.
### :see: {Containers-And-Iterators}
routine back_resolve(count: U64, offset: U64) -> U64
  if offset > count
    throw IndexOutOfBoundsError(index: offset, count: count)
  return count -% offset
